  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This 4-star campsite of the Tikayan chain, between the village of Grimaud and the lakeside town of Port Grimaud, has rentals only: 104 air-conditioned mobile homes for 1 to 8 people, no bare pitches. The beaches of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez are 4 km away, Saint-Tropez 10 km. A 670 m² pool is open from April to September.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The campsite's official website states "dog under 40 kg allowed" for the Standard and Comfort ranges. Category 1 and 2 dogs are not accepted, the vaccination record must be up to date and the dog must be kept on a leash in the campsite (campsite text relayed by Tourisme avec mon chien). The campsite states there that it accepts up to two animals; some booking platforms count only one per rental. A small gift (poop bags, bowl, toy) awaits the dog on arrival, according to the same text.</p>
      <p>The supplement is payable on site: 3 € per day in low season and 6 € in high season according to that text, 5 € per day according to other platforms. The campsite is open from 2 April to 7 November 2027; the reception office answers Monday to Friday from 9 am to 12 pm and from 2 pm to 6 pm on 04 94 43 26 95.</p>

      <h2>Check before you go</h2>
      <p>Amount of the supplement and number of dogs admitted per rental (different versions depending on the sources): to be confirmed with the campsite when booking.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The campsite's text mentions gulf beaches open to dogs a few minutes away (Ramatuelle, Sainte-Maxime); the rules of each beach vary by town and season, to be checked with the town before you go.</p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Official Tikayan website (campsite page), Tourisme avec mon chien, Maeva, Selectour, read on 12/11/2026.</p>
